    <h2>1. What is a Variable?</h2>
    <p><b>Variable = A Box / Container</b> where we store data. The box has a <b>name</b> and inside it there is a <b>value</b>.</p>
    <p>Example: There is a box. On the box it says <b>"name"</b>, and inside it is <b>"Ali"</b>. Whenever we need Ali, we call the box by its name - <b>name</b>.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Real Life Example:</b> In school, every student has a Roll Number. Roll Number = Variable Name, Student Name = Value. The teacher calls the Roll Number, and the student stands up. The same thing happens in JS.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Variables in Action</h2>
    <p>Type your name and press the button. This works with variables:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <h3 id="demoGreet" style="margin:0">Hello, Guest! 👋</h3>
      <p style="color:#64748b;margin:8px 0">Your Age: <b id="demoAge">-</b> | Your Score: <b id="demoScore">0</b></p>
      <input class="demo-input" id="nameInput" type="text" placeholder="Type your name - e.g. Ali">
      <input class="demo-input" id="ageInput" type="number" placeholder="Type your age - e.g. 20">
      <button class="btn btn-js" onclick="saveData()">Save My Data 💾</button>
      <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="addScore()">+10 Score ⭐</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="resetDemo()">Reset ↺</button>
    </div>
    <h2>3. How to Create a Variable? - 3 Ways</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Way 1 - let (Most Used - Value can change)</span><br>
<span class="text">let name = "Ali";</span><br>
<span class="text">let age = 20;</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Way 2 - const (Value can NOT change)</span><br>
<span class="text">const country = "Pakistan";</span><br>
<span class="text">const pi = 3.14;</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Way 3 - var (Old Way - Do not use now)</span><br>
<span class="text">var city = "Lahore";</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>4. let vs const vs var - Full Difference</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Feature</th><th>let</th><th>const</th><th>var</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Value Change?</td><td>✅ Yes, can change</td><td>❌ No, fixed</td><td>✅ Yes, can change</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Use Today?</td><td>✅ YES - Most used</td><td>✅ YES - For fixed values</td><td>❌ NO - Old, avoid</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Example</td><td>let age = 20; age = 21;</td><td>const pi = 3.14;</td><td>var x = 10;</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Re-declare?</td><td>❌ No</td><td>❌ No</td><td>✅ Yes (Problem!)</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="note"><b>Golden Rule:</b> Always use <b>let</b> if the value will change (age, score, count). Use <b>const</b> if the value will never change (country, pi, website name). Forget <b>var</b>.</div>
    <h2>5. Change Value - let Example</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let score = 0;</span><br>
<span class="text">score = 10; // ✅ Allowed - let can change</span><br>
<span class="text">score = 20; // ✅ Allowed</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(score); // Output: 20</span><br><br>
<span class="text">const name = "Ali";</span><br>
<span class="text">name = "Ahmed"; // ❌ ERROR - const cannot change</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. Rules for Naming Variables</h2>
    <p>1. <b>Start with letter, _ or $</b> - <code>let name</code> ✅, <code>let 1name</code> ❌<br>2. <b>No Space</b> - <code>let myName</code> ✅, <code>let my name</code> ❌<br>3. <b>Case Sensitive</b> - <code>Name</code> and <code>name</code> are different.<br>4. <b>No Reserved Words</b> - You cannot use <code>let, const, var, function</code> as a name.<br>5. <b>Use camelCase</b> - <code>myName, totalPrice, userAge</code> - First word small, first letter of next words capital.</p>
    <h2>7. Complete Example - Copy and Try in Playground</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"result"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">My Data</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"showData()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Show My Data</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let name = "Ali";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let age = 20;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">const country = "Pakistan";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let score = 0;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function showData() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">score = score + 10;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("result").innerHTML = "Name: " + name + " | Age: " + age + " | Country: " + country + " | Score: " + score;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Understand this:</b> In <code>"Name: " + name</code>, the <b>+</b> means <b>Join</b>. It joins Text + Variable. This is called <b>Concatenation</b>.</p>
    <h2>8. Common Mistakes</h2>
    <p>1. <b>Changing const:</b> <code>const x = 5; x = 10;</code> ❌ This will give an error.<br>2. <b>Forgetting Quotes:</b> <code>let name = Ali;</code> ❌ - JS will think Ali is a variable. Correct is <code>let name = "Ali";</code> ✅<br>3. <b>Space in name:</b> <code>let my name</code> ❌<br>4. <b>Starting with Number:</b> <code>let 2age</code> ❌</p>
    <h2>9. Homework</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build this:</p>
    <p>1. <code>let myName = "Your Name"</code>, <code>let myAge = Your Age</code>, <code>const myCountry = "Your Country"</code><br>2. One button - on click, show in <code>innerHTML</code>: "My Name is ___ , Age ___ , Country ___"<br>3. One <code>let count = 0</code>, on button click do <code>count = count + 1</code> and show it on the screen</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Variable = Box to store data | let = Can change | const = Cannot change | var = Old, do not use | Naming = camelCase, no space, no number at start | + = Join text + variable | "Ali" = Text needs quotes, 20 = Number, no quotes</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson23">Lesson 23 - Data Types & Operators</a> - Learn what Number, String, Boolean are, and how + - * / work.</p>
